# Line endings are not cosmetic here. A shell script checked out with CRLF fails
# on Linux with "bash: \r: command not found", which points at nothing, and the
# firmware and SQL are read by tools that are equally unforgiving.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
# The opposite rule for Windows scripts. cmd.exe resolves `goto` labels by
# scanning lines, and with LF-only endings it can miss them; gradlew.bat uses
# several, so a clone on Windows would fail to build with no useful message.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
